1928-01-01 00:00:00 from UT+7:45:40 to UT+8.#@2 #@60 Name of location used for calculation of Chinese calendar.#@103 Minutes difference between daylight saving and standard time.
Default is for no daylight saving time.#@172 Abbreviated name of standard time zone used for Chinese calendar.
This is an expression depending on `year' because it changed
at 1928-01-01 00:00:00 from `PMT' to `CST'.#@74 Abbreviated name of daylight saving time zone used for Chinese calendar.#@158 Sexp giving the date on which daylight saving time starts.
Default is for no daylight saving time.  See documentation of
`calendar-daylight-savings-starts'.#@154 Sexp giving the date on which daylight saving time ends.
Default is for no daylight saving time.  See documentation of
`calendar-daylight-savings-ends'.#@108 Number of minutes after midnight that daylight saving time starts.
Default is for no daylight saving time.#@106 Number of minutes after midnight that daylight saving time ends.
Default is for no daylight saving time.#@55 Prefixes used by `calendar-chinese-sexagesimal-name'.#@55 Suffixes used by `calendar-chinese-sexagesimal-name'.#@184 The N-th name of the Chinese sexagesimal cycle.
N congruent to 1 gives the first name, N congruent to 2 gives the second name,
..., N congruent to 60 gives the sixtieth name.

