#@211 Which conses/vectors/records have been processed in strip-symbol-positions?
The value is a hash table, the keys being the elements and the values being t.

The purpose of this is to detect circular structures.
(defvar byte-run--ssp-seen nil (#$ . 84))#@133 Strip the positions from symbols with position in the list ARG.
This is done by destructively modifying ARG.  Return ARG.

(fn ARG)
(defalias 'byte-run--strip-list #[257 "\211\301\"\204J␀\302\303#\210\304@!\203␀\211\305@!\240\210\202@␀\211@:\203-␀\306@!\210\202@␀\307@!\204;␀\310@!\203@␀\311@!\210\211A:\203J␀A\202␀\304A!\203[␀\211\305A!\241\210\202n␀\307A!\204i␀\310A!\203n␀\311A!\210\207" [byte-run--ssp-seen gethash puthash t symbol-with-pos-p bare-symbol byte-run--strip-list vectorp recordp byte-run--strip-vector/record] 6 (#$ . 342)])#@142 Strip the positions from symbols with position in the vector/record ARG.
This is done by destructively modifying ARG.  Return ARG.

(fn ARG)
