(defalias 'cl-once-only '(macro . #[385 "\300\301\"\262\302\211:\203␀@\262\303 B\262A\262\202	␀\266\202\237\304\302\211:\203=␀@\262\305BB\262A\262\202&␀\266\202\237\306\304\307\310\302\302\211\211\211:\203\206␀@\262:\203\206␀@\262A@\206i␀@\262\306\307D\307DDDB\262A\262A\262\210\302\202M␀\210\266\205\237BD\307\304	\302	\302\211:\203\272␀@\262:\203\272␀@\262@DB\262A\262A\262\202\225␀\266\204\237	BBDEDE\207" [mapcar ensure-list nil gensym let ((gensym)) \` \, list] 20 (#$ . 59503)]))#@393 Collect multiple return values.
FORM must return a list; the BODY is then executed with the first N elements
of this list bound (`let'-style) to each of the symbols SYM in turn.  This
is analogous to the Common Lisp `multiple-value-bind' macro, using lists to
