#@117 Don't try to update copyright beyond this position unless interactive.
A value of nil means to search whole buffer.#@2 #@108 Non-nil means to search backwards from the end of the buffer for copyright.
This is useful for ChangeLogs.#@89 What your copyright notice looks like.
The second \( \) construct must match the years.#@257 Regexp matching the names which correspond to the user.
Only copyright lines where the name matches this regexp will be updated.
This allows you to avoid adding years to a copyright notice belonging to
someone else or to a group for which you do not work.#@91 Match additional copyright notice years.
The second \( \) construct must match the years.#@275 Non-nil if individual consecutive years should be replaced with a range.
For example: 2005, 2006, 2007, 2008 might be replaced with 2005-2008.
If you use ranges, you should add an explanatory note in a README file.
