#@338 Prefix that is ignored before the tag.
For example, you can write the 1st line synopsis string and headers like this
in your Lisp package:

   ;; @(#) package.el -- package description
   ;;
   ;; @(#) $Maintainer:   Person Foo Bar $

The @(#) construct is used by unix what(1) and
then $identifier: doc string $ is used by GNU ident(1)#@2 #@128 Prefix that is ignored before the dates in a copyright.
Leading comment characters and whitespace should be in regexp group 1.#@43 Column used for placing formatted output.#@44 Regexp which matches start of any section.#@54 Regexp which matches start of documentation section.#@53 Regexp which matches the start of code log section.#@150 Return regexp for matching HEADER.
