(fn MAP KEY &optional TESTFN)#@160 Return non-nil if MAP contains KEY.
If MAP is an alist, TESTFN defaults to `equal'.
If MAP is a plist, TESTFN defaults to `eq'.

(fn MAP KEY &optional TESTFN)#@91 Return non-nil if KEY is an index of MAP, ignoring TESTFN.

(fn MAP KEY &optional TESTFN)#@85 Return non-nil if MAP contains KEY, ignoring TESTFN.

(fn MAP KEY &optional TESTFN)#@248 Return the first non-nil value from applying PRED to elements of MAP.
Return nil if no such element is found.
PRED is called with two arguments: the key of an element and its value.
The default implementation delegates to `map-do'.

(fn PRED MAP)#@18 

(fn KEY VALUE)#@209 Return non-nil if calling PRED on all elements of MAP returns non-nil.
PRED is called with two arguments: the key of an element and its value.
The default implementation delegates to `map-do'.

(fn PRED MAP)#@248 Merge into a map of TYPE all the key/value pairs in MAPS.
MERGE is a function that takes the target MAP, a KEY and its
VALUE, merges KEY and VALUE into MAP, and returns the result.
MAP may be of a type other than TYPE.

(fn MERGE TYPE &rest MAPS)
