(defvar describe-symbol-backends (byte-code "\300\301\302E\300\303\304E\305\306\307E\310\311\312EF\207" [nil fboundp #[771 "\300!\207" [describe-function] 5 (#$ . 17870)] #[257 "\300!\203␀\301!?\206␀\211\302N\207" [boundp keywordp variable-documentation] 3 (#$ . 17888)] describe-variable "type" cl-find-class cl-describe-type "face" facep #[771 "\300!\207" [describe-face] 5 (#$ . 17870)]] 6) (#$ . 17397))#@48 If non-nil, remove quotes around link buttons.#@978 Parse and hyperlink documentation cross-references in the given BUFFER.

Find cross-reference information in a buffer and activate such cross
references for selection with `help-follow-symbol'.  Cross-references have
the canonical form `...'  and the type of reference may be
disambiguated by the preceding word(s) used in
`help-xref-symbol-regexp'.  Faces only get cross-referenced if
preceded or followed by the word `face'.  Variables without
variable documentation do not get cross-referenced, unless
preceded by the word `variable' or `option'.

If the variable `help-xref-mule-regexp' is non-nil, find also
cross-reference information related to multilingual environment
(e.g., coding-systems).  This variable is also used to disambiguate
the type of reference as the same way as `help-xref-symbol-regexp'.

A special reference `back' is made to return back through a stack of
help buffers.  Variable `help-back-label' specifies the text for
that.

(fn &optional BUFFER)#@10 

