Otherwise buffers whose name matches an element of
`ibuffer-never-search-content-name' or whose major mode is on
`ibuffer-never-search-content-mode' are excluded.

(fn REGEXP &optional ALL-BUFFERS)#@59 Mark all buffers whose major mode equals MODE.

(fn MODE)#@28 Mark all modified buffers.#@57 Mark all modified buffers that have an associated file.#@56 Mark all buffers whose associated file does not exist.#@75 Mark buffers whose major mode is in variable `ibuffer-help-buffer-modes'.#@51 Mark buffers whose associated file is compressed.#@70 Mark buffers which have not been viewed in `ibuffer-old-time' hours.#@55 Mark all buffers whose name begins and ends with `*'.#@29 Mark all read-only buffers.#@27 Mark all `dired' buffers.#@172 View lines which match REGEXP in all marked buffers.
Optional argument NLINES says how many lines of context to display: it
defaults to one.

(fn REGEXP &optional NLINES)
