#@70 String used by Icomplete to separate alternatives in the minibuffer.#@2 #@97 When non-nil, hide common prefix from completion candidates.
When nil, show candidates in full.#@239 If non-nil, automatically delete superfluous parts of file names.
For example, if the user types ~/ after a long path name,
everything preceding the ~/ is discarded so the interactive
selection process starts again from the user's $HOME.#@402 When non-nil, show completions when first prompting for input.
This means to show completions even when the current minibuffer contents
is the same as was the initial input after minibuffer activation.
This also means that if you traverse the list of completions with
commands like \`C-.' and just hit \`RET' without typing any
characters, the match under point will be chosen instead of the
default.#@243 Specialized completion tables with which Icomplete should operate.
If this is t, Icomplete operates on all tables.
Otherwise this should be a list of the completion tables (e.g.,
`internal-complete-buffer') on which Icomplete should operate.#@70 Format of the current/total number of matches for the prompt prefix.#@54 Face used by Icomplete for highlighting first match.
