identification number of the table respectively.  It also registers
the table in `translation-table-vector'.

(fn SYMBOL &rest ARGS)
(defalias 'define-translation-table #[385 "\301@!\203␀\302@!\303=\203␀\211@\202␀\304\305\"G\306\307\310\303#\210\211\204\\␀Y\2037␀\311\312\307\"\"H\211\203F␀\211@=\203T␀BI\266\313\202%␀T\262\210\202%␀\310\314#\210\207" [translation-table-vector char-table-p char-table-subtype translation-table apply make-translation-table 0 nil put vconcat make-vector t translation-table-id] 11 (#$ . 68248)])#@355 From START to END, translate characters according to TABLE.
TABLE is a string or a char-table.
If TABLE is a string, the Nth character in it is the mapping
