#@92 The mouse event used by kmacro to call a macro.
Set to nil if no mouse binding is desired.#@2 #@58 Maximum number of keyboard macros to save in macro ring.#@422 Controls whether appending to a macro starts by executing the macro.
If non-nil, using a single \[universal-argument] prefix executes the macro
before appending, while more than one \[universal-argument] prefix does not
execute the macro.
Otherwise, a single \[universal-argument] prefix does not execute the
macro, while more than one \[universal-argument] prefix causes the
macro to be executed before appending to it.#@86 Allow repeating certain macro commands without entering the \[kmacro-keymap] prefix.#@62 Allow repeating macro call using last key or a specific key.#@71 Repeat macro call with original arg when non-nil; repeat once if nil.#@66 Override `max-mini-window-height' when step edit keyboard macro.#@37 Keymap for keyboard macro commands.
