(fn FILE &optional DO-NOT-KILL-BUFFER-WHEN-DONE)#@542 Generate and print a PostScript syntactic chart image of the buffer.

When called with a numeric prefix argument (\[universal-argument]), prompts the user for
the name of a file to save the PostScript image in, instead of sending
it to the printer.

More specifically, the FILENAME argument is treated as follows: if it
is nil, send the image to the printer.  If FILENAME is a string, save
the PostScript image in a file with that name.  If FILENAME is a
number, prompt the user for the name of the file to save in.

(fn &optional FILENAME)#@165 Generate and print a PostScript syntactic chart image of the region.
