(fn &optional INTERACTIVELY)#@51 If cycling completion is in use, cycle backwards.#@88 Expand the textual value of the current argument.
This will modify the current buffer.#@56 Complete without reference to any cycling completions.#@64 Display any help information relative to the current argument.#@65 Show the list of possible completions for the current argument.#@213 Setup a comint buffer to use pcomplete.
COMPLETEF-SYM should be the symbol where the
dynamic-complete-functions are kept.  For comint mode itself,
this is `comint-dynamic-complete-functions'.

(fn COMPLETEF-SYM)#@38 Setup `shell-mode' to use pcomplete.#@226 Run a `cvs checkout MODULES' in DIR.
Feed the output to a *cvs* buffer, display it in the current window,
and run `cvs-mode' on it.

With a prefix argument, prompt for cvs FLAGS to use.

(fn MODULES DIR FLAGS &optional ROOT)#@337 Open a *cvs* buffer on DIR without running cvs.
With a prefix argument, prompt for a directory to use.
A prefix arg >8 (ex: \[universal-argument] \[universal-argument]),
  prevents reuse of an existing *cvs* buffer.
Optional argument NOSHOW if non-nil means not to display the buffer.
FLAGS is ignored.

(fn DIR &optional FLAGS NOSHOW)#@466 Run a `cvs -n update' in the specified DIRECTORY.
That is, check what needs to be done, but don't change the disc.
Feed the output to a *cvs* buffer and run `cvs-mode' on it.
With a prefix argument, prompt for a directory and cvs FLAGS to use.
A prefix arg >8 (ex: \[universal-argument] \[universal-argument]),
  prevents reuse of an existing *cvs* buffer.
Optional argument NOSHOW if non-nil means not to display the buffer.

(fn DIRECTORY FLAGS &optional NOSHOW)#@410 Run a `cvs update' in the current working DIRECTORY.
Feed the output to a *cvs* buffer and run `cvs-mode' on it.
With a \[universal-argument] prefix argument, prompt for a directory to use.
A prefix arg >8 (ex: \[universal-argument] \[universal-argument]),
  prevents reuse of an existing *cvs* buffer.
The prefix is also passed to `cvs-flags-query' to select the FLAGS
  passed to cvs.

(fn DIRECTORY FLAGS)#@404 Run a `cvs status' in the current working DIRECTORY.
Feed the output to a *cvs* buffer and run `cvs-mode' on it.
With a prefix argument, prompt for a directory and cvs FLAGS to use.
A prefix arg >8 (ex: \[universal-argument] \[universal-argument]),
  prevents reuse of an existing *cvs* buffer.
Optional argument NOSHOW if non-nil means not to display the buffer.

(fn DIRECTORY FLAGS &optional NOSHOW)#@126 The action to be performed when opening a CVS directory.
Sensible values are `cvs-examine', `cvs-status' and `cvs-quickdir'.
