#@175 Whether to call the Un*x "man" program synchronously.
When this is non-nil, call the "man" program synchronously
(rather than asynchronously, which is the default behavior).#@2 #@160 Whether to call the Un*x "man" program on remote systems.
When this is non-nil, call the "man" program on the remote
system determined by `default-directory'.#@433 Manpage cleaning filter command phrases.
This variable contains a list of the following form:

  ((command-string phrase-string*)*)

Each phrase-string is concatenated onto the command-string to form a
command filter.  The (standard) output (and standard error) of the Un*x
man command is piped through each command filter in the order the
commands appear in the association list.  The final output is placed in
the manpage buffer.#@65 Non-nil means use `untabify' instead of `Man-untabify-command'.
(byte-code "\300\301!\210\300\302!\210\303\304\305\306\307\310\311\312\311\313&	\210\314\315\316\317\320DD\321\322\323\311\304\324\325&	\210\314\326\316\317\327DD\330\322\323\324\325&\210\314\331\316\317\332DD\333\322\334\311\304&\207" [require ansi-color cl-lib custom-declare-group man nil "Browse UNIX manual pages." :prefix "Man-" :group external help custom-declare-variable Man-prefer-synchronous-call funcall function #[0 "\300\207" [nil] 1 (#$ . 262)] (#$ . 84) :type boolean :version "30.1" Man-support-remote-systems #[0 "\300\207" [nil] 1 (#$ . 262)] (#$ . 269) Man-filter-list #[0 "\300\207" [nil] 1 (#$ . 262)] (#$ . 434) (repeat (list (string :tag "Command String") (repeat :inline t (string :tag "Phrase String"))))] 10)
