#@60 If non-nil, a string naming the group file on your system.#@2 #@61 If non-nil, a string naming the passwd file on your system.#@336 If non-nil, a string naming your SSH "known_hosts" file.
This allows one method of completion of SSH host names, the other
being via `pcmpl-ssh-config-file'.  Note that newer versions of
ssh hash the hosts by default, to prevent Island-hopping SSH
attacks.  This can be disabled, at some risk, with the SSH option
"HashKnownHosts no".#@159 If non-nil, a string naming your SSH "config" file.
