(defvar reveal-mode nil (#$ . 3522))#@764 Toggle uncloaking of invisible text near point (Reveal mode).

Reveal mode is a buffer-local minor mode.  When enabled, it
reveals invisible text around point.

Also see the `reveal-auto-hide' variable.

This is a minor mode.  If called interactively, toggle the `Reveal mode'
mode.  If the prefix argument is positive, enable the mode, and if it is
zero or negative, disable the mode.

If called from Lisp, toggle the mode if ARG is `toggle'.  Enable the
mode if ARG is nil, omitted, or is a positive number.  Disable the mode
if ARG is a negative number.

To check whether the minor mode is enabled in the current buffer,
evaluate the variable `reveal-mode'.

The mode's hook is called both when the mode is enabled and when it is
disabled.

(fn &optional ARG)
(make-variable-buffer-local 'reveal-mode)
(defalias 'reveal-mode #[256 "\303 \304=\203␀?\202␀\247\203␀\305W\203␀\306\202␀\307\310\301!\2031␀\311\300	\"\2031␀\300	B\203E␀\312\302!\210\307\313\314\315\306\307$\210\202O␀\316\302!\210\317\314\315\307#\210\320\321\203Y␀\322\202Z␀\323\"\210\324\325!\203}␀\303 \203n␀\211\303 \232\203}␀\326\327\330\203y␀\331\202z␀\332\333$\210\210\334 \207" [reveal-mode local-minor-modes search-invisible current-message toggle 1 nil t boundp delq make-local-variable add-hook post-command-hook reveal-post-command kill-local-variable remove-hook run-hooks reveal-mode-hook reveal-mode-on-hook reveal-mode-off-hook called-interactively-p any message "%s %sabled%s" "Reveal mode" "en" "dis" " in current buffer" force-mode-line-update] 8 (#$ . 3655) (byte-code "\203\n␀\301!\202␀\302C\207" [current-prefix-arg prefix-numeric-value toggle] 2)])
(defvar reveal-mode-hook nil)#@275 Non-nil if Global Reveal mode is enabled.
See the `global-reveal-mode' command
for a description of this minor mode.
Setting this variable directly does not take effect;
either customize it (see the info node `Easy Customization')
or call the function `global-reveal-mode'.#@708 Toggle Reveal mode in all buffers (Global Reveal mode).

Reveal mode renders invisible text around point visible again.

This is a global minor mode.  If called interactively, toggle the
`Global Reveal mode' mode.  If the prefix argument is positive, enable
the mode, and if it is zero or negative, disable the mode.

If called from Lisp, toggle the mode if ARG is `toggle'.  Enable the
mode if ARG is nil, omitted, or is a positive number.  Disable the mode
if ARG is a negative number.

To check whether the minor mode is enabled in the current buffer,
evaluate `(default-value \='global-reveal-mode)'.

The mode's hook is called both when the mode is enabled and when it is
disabled.

