(fn OBJ)#@73 Format OBJ's `description' for display and return the result.

(fn OBJ)#@181 The `description' slot may be a function, in which case that is
called inside the correct buffer (see `transient--insert-group')
and its value is returned to the caller.

(fn OBJ)#@180 Format the description by calling the next method.
If the result doesn't use the `face' property at all, then apply the
face `transient-heading' to the complete string.

(fn OBJ)#@250 Format the description by calling the next method.
If the result is nil, then use "(BUG: no description)" as the
description.
If the OBJ's `key' is currently unreachable, then apply the face
`transient-unreachable' to the complete string.

(fn OBJ)#@65 Format OBJ's value for display and return the result.

