#@59 A regular expression specifying local hostnames/machines.#@2 #@47 A regular expression matching a shell prompt.#@60 What hostname to actually rlog into before doing a telnet.#@65 Username to log into the remote machine with when using rlogin.#@93 Parameters to `url-open-rlogin'.
This list will be used as the parameter list given to rsh.#@59 What hostname to actually login to before doing a telnet.#@103 Parameters to `url-open-telnet'.
This list will be executed as a command after logging in via telnet.#@76 Prompt that tells us we should send our username when logging in w/telnet.#@76 Prompt that tells us we should send our password when logging in w/telnet.#@38 User name to log in via telnet with.#@44 Password to use to log in via telnet with.#@322 Whether to use nslookup to resolve hostnames.
This should be used when your version of Emacs cannot correctly
use DNS, but your machine can.

This used to happen on SunOS 4.x and Ultrix when Emacs was linked
statically, and also was not linked with the resolver libraries.
Those systems are no longer supported by Emacs.#@51 If non-nil then a string naming nslookup program.#@74 Attempt to resolve the given HOST using nslookup if possible.

